%% DM26-0670

%% A credential from the sops file to the request that presents it, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/signed-configuration.md, "Secrets in a document",
%% docs/architecture/jira.md, "The credential", docs/architecture/protocol-handlers.md). jira-observer and git-repo-observer declare one. The domain never holds it.
%% The request itself is general/protocol_handler_request. Tested, and not presented to a real site on a cluster in this pass: u7s reads Jira anonymously and has
%% no credential in either section. Rotating the escrow key is general/key_rotation, the one place LoadSecret has a use, and it is not built.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Author as Author, or the seed from sops
    participant Sign as polar-sign
    participant Front as Credentials observer<br/>(its gateway)
    participant Config as ConfigurationActor
    participant Handler as Protocol handler
    participant Crypto as CryptoActor
    participant Daemon as Custody daemon
    participant CA as Credentials agent
    participant Domain as The agent's domain

    Note over Author,Sign: Sealed once on a fresh cluster, by the seed.<br/>After that a new token is an author's,<br/>at a higher version
    Author->>Sign: sign the section, the secret on standard input
    Sign->>Front: POST /agent-escrow-key { identity }
    Front-->>Sign: the agent's escrow certificate, which is public
    Sign->>Sign: it chains to the author's CA, is valid now, may be sealed to,<br/>and names this agent. Only then seal, then sign
    Note over Sign: Each secret is an EscrowedSecret bound to<br/>agent|credentials|version|name|secret,<br/>with its host_pattern beside it
    Sign->>Config: pushed to polar-schedules, then delivered (signed_configuration_delivery)

    Config->>Config: verify the document, judge the shape of the section, open nothing
    Config->>Config: replace the section if the version is above its last
    Config-)Handler: RuntimeChanged
    Handler->>Config: the section in force. A version it has handled is no news
    loop each entry
        Handler->>Crypto: RegisterSecret { name, section, secret, context, binding }
        Crypto->>Crypto: the binding is usable, and the bytes are an escrowed secret
        Crypto->>Daemon: unwrap, with the escrow key that never leaves it
        Daemon-->>Crypto: the secret's own key
        Crypto->>Crypto: open under the context, keep with its binding
        Crypto-->>Handler: registered, or why not, and nothing is kept
    end
    Handler->>Crypto: ReplaceSection { section, keep }
    Crypto->>Crypto: drop what this version leaves out, and stop escrowing it
    Crypto-->>Handler: the names withdrawn
    alt an entry failed
        Handler->>Handler: hold Credentials, by name and reason
    else every entry registered
        Handler->>Handler: release the hold, and forget what the site refused
    end
    Handler-)Domain: CredentialsApplied { version, registered, failed, withdrawn }

    Note over Crypto,CA: In the background, retried with a growing wait until acknowledged.<br/>A refusal that trying again cannot change is logged and ends it
    Crypto->>CA: EscrowKeyRequest, then StoreSecret, the secret and its binding, labelled with its kind
    CA-->>Crypto: stored

    Domain->>Handler: an operation, which names no credential value
    Handler->>Handler: judge it (protocol_handler_request)
    Handler->>Crypto: UseCredential { pass, Http or Git { name, host } }
    Crypto->>Crypto: only the handlers' pass, and the host must fit the binding
    Crypto-->>Handler: what that protocol presents
    Handler->>Handler: present it, once, for this request
    Handler-->>Domain: the result, never the credential

    Note over Handler,Daemon: A restart in place forgets every secret. Replay brings the same signed document back,<br/>the section's version starts again from zero, and the custodian has fetched<br/>the identity's escrow key again, so it opens, from the first loop above
    Note over Crypto,CA: The copy with the credentials agent is not read back.<br/>RetrieveSecret refuses a credential's own record (IsACredential),<br/>and LoadSecret has no caller yet. A version that withdraws<br/>an entry leaves that copy there, since the ledger has no delete
